   101	**Proof.** For every fixed radius R, the two inclusion errors tend to zero. For instance, a sequence of bounded points of either set is within an error tending to zero of points of the other. Both limit inclusion criteria therefore agree. Rotations are used only as an isometric change of frame in this comparison; Lambda_j is already in physical coordinates. QED.
