   271	## 4. Main theorem and exact scope
   272	
   273	**Theorem 4.1 (generic paired three-super-soliton obstruction).** For every integer
   274	n≥4, the Wang–Tang–Liang paired supersymmetric system
   275	
   276	    P_n F·G=0,       S_y P_n F·G=0
   277	
   278	has no three-super-soliton family with generic independent F–F–G body data in the
   279	class of §1.2. In particular it fails the generic all-allowed-pattern criterion,
   280	including the independent two-amplitude interpretation at odd n. This remains true
   281	with arbitrary nilpotent interaction dressings and extra body-zero terms in F,G.
